1
00:00:01,130 --> 00:00:04,940
Here's a timeline we built
of artificial intelligence,

2
00:00:04,990 --> 00:00:11,320
from a philosopher's paper wheels around
1300 to the language models of today.

3
00:00:11,370 --> 00:00:15,050
Programs, machines, papers
and policy are moments,

4
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:19,010
each linked to its sources, and the
field's eras are bands behind them,

5
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,989
two of them winters.

6
00:00:22,539 --> 00:00:27,769
Long before computers, people
imagined reasoning as calculation.

7
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:31,909
Leibniz hoped arguments could
be settled by computing.

8
00:00:31,959 --> 00:00:35,779
Ada Lovelace saw that Babbage's
engine could work with symbols,

9
00:00:35,829 --> 00:00:40,269
not just numbers. Boole
turned logic into algebra,

10
00:00:40,319 --> 00:00:45,119
and in 1936 Alan Turing described
a machine that could carry out any

11
00:00:45,169 --> 00:00:46,770
computation.

12
00:00:48,210 --> 00:00:52,940
In 1950, Turing asked
whether machines can think.

13
00:00:52,990 --> 00:00:57,040
Six years later, a summer workshop at
Dartmouth gave the field its name,

14
00:00:57,090 --> 00:01:00,850
and the golden years began:
programs that proved theorems,

15
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:04,480
the language LISP, ELIZA's
conversations, and Shakey,

16
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:07,477
a robot that planned its own moves.

17
00:01:09,017 --> 00:01:12,967
Open a moment to read it: what
happened, how sure its date is,

18
00:01:13,017 --> 00:01:16,967
its picture's credit, and
the article it comes from.

19
00:01:17,017 --> 00:01:19,381
Every moment here has its sources.

20
00:01:21,111 --> 00:01:26,181
Then the bands turn cold.
Promises outran results;

21
00:01:26,231 --> 00:01:30,701
after Britain's Lighthill report
in 1973, funding was cut,

22
00:01:30,751 --> 00:01:37,061
and the first AI winter set in. Expert
systems brought a boom in the 1980s,

23
00:01:37,111 --> 00:01:42,301
with rules written by hand, until cheaper
workstations undercut AI's special

24
00:01:42,351 --> 00:01:45,048
machines and a second winter followed.

25
00:01:46,598 --> 00:01:51,498
Now pull one thread. Separate by
tags, choose neural networks,

26
00:01:51,548 --> 00:01:58,288
and one idea rises into its own track.
1943: a model of the neuron as logic.

27
00:01:58,338 --> 00:02:02,788
1958: Rosenblatt's perceptron
learns from examples.

28
00:02:02,838 --> 00:02:08,748
1969: a book proves its limits, and the
track goes quiet for over a decade.

29
00:02:08,798 --> 00:02:15,298
1986: backpropagation trains deeper
networks. And still they wait.

30
00:02:16,968 --> 00:02:21,898
Here's what the line makes visible. The
artificial neuron is older than the

31
00:02:21,948 --> 00:02:25,733
transistor, and it took
sixty-nine years to win.

32
00:02:27,193 --> 00:02:32,043
In 2012, a network trained on graphics
cards won the ImageNet challenge by a

33
00:02:32,093 --> 00:02:37,263
wide margin, and the bands
change: deep learning.

34
00:02:37,313 --> 00:02:40,498
Four years later, AlphaGo
beat Lee Sedol at Go.

35
00:02:41,958 --> 00:02:46,468
In 2017, researchers at Google
published the Transformer,

36
00:02:46,518 --> 00:02:50,478
built on attention. Language
models grew from it,

37
00:02:50,528 --> 00:02:57,223
larger each year, and in November 2022,
ChatGPT put one in front of the public.

38
00:02:58,773 --> 00:03:04,113
Zoom in to the days. By the end of
2023 there were models from Meta,

39
00:03:04,163 --> 00:03:09,793
OpenAI, Anthropic and Google; an
open letter asking for a pause;

40
00:03:09,843 --> 00:03:14,003
a statement on extinction risk;
an American executive order;

41
00:03:14,053 --> 00:03:19,263
and a summit at Bletchley Park. Researchers
disagree about how fast this is

42
00:03:19,313 --> 00:03:24,318
moving and what it means; the timeline
keeps each step with its source.

43
00:03:25,798 --> 00:03:31,408
In 2024, Nobel prizes went to work on
neural networks and to the makers of

44
00:03:31,458 --> 00:03:36,598
AlphaFold, and Europe's
AI Act came into force.

45
00:03:36,648 --> 00:03:40,368
The line is still being
written. Anyone can read it,

46
00:03:40,418 --> 00:03:43,525
no account needed, and
anyone can build one.
